# ============================================================================
# MATRIX — .gitignore
#
# Policy: commit CODE, CONFIG, CHECKPOINTS and RESULTS. Ignore RAW and DERIVED
# DATA, which is large and regenerable by the pass1..pass12 pipeline.
#
# This keeps the repo at roughly 20 MB instead of 605 MB and avoids GitHub's
# 50 MB per-file warning / 100 MB hard limit.
#
# KEPT deliberately (small but essential):
#   *.pt checkpoints (14 files, ~8 MB)      the actual frozen models
#   scaler.json / scaler.npz                train-only normalisation statistics
#   split_manifest.csv, metadata/*.parquet  which session is in which split
#   feature_schema.json, *.yaml, *.json     frozen configuration records
#   all reports, metrics and result CSVs
#
# See model/RUN.md Section 16 for how to regenerate everything ignored here.
# ============================================================================

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
env/
.Python
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- OS / editor -------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp

# ============================================================================
# RAW DATASET — 2.1 GB. Obtain IO-VNBD separately, see model/RUN.md.
# ============================================================================
model/dataset/

# ============================================================================
# DERIVED DATA — regenerable, ~577 MB. Do not commit.
# ============================================================================

# ML training arrays (X_ext_train.npy alone is 107 MB, X_train.npy 58 MB).
# Regenerate: model/preprocessing/pass12_build_training.py
# NOTE: scaler.npz is .npz, not .npy, so it is NOT matched by this rule.
*.npy

# Per-session canonical parquet. Regenerate: pass8_build.py
model/preprocessing/smartphone_core/
model/preprocessing/smartphone_enhanced/
model/preprocessing/vehicle_reference/

# Per-session targets. Regenerate: pass11_targets.py
model/preprocessing/targets/

# Stationary calibration parquet — but KEEP sensor_bias_estimates.csv,
# which inference needs for per-session bias correction.
model/preprocessing/calibration/*.parquet

# Dense stride-1 predictions. Regenerate: complementary_fusion/generate_dense.py
model/experiments/complementary_fusion/predictions/dense/
model/experiments/delta_v/predictions/dense_*.parquet
model/experiments/delta_v/targets/*.parquet

# Intermediate scan artefacts (pass1/pass2) — large JSON, regenerable.
# pass1_files.json is also the raw-integrity manifest; drop the ignore line
# below if you want to keep that check available on a fresh clone.
model/preprocessing/outputs/pass2_fp.json

# Scratch / ad-hoc analysis leftovers
model/preprocessing/outputs/_*.csv

# ============================================================================
# Node / Expo (mobile app) — mobile/.gitignore also covers these
# ============================================================================
node_modules/
.expo/
dist/
web-build/

# ============================================================================
# Logs
# ============================================================================
*.log
train.log
